# Every attack of the program tests/programs/attack.asm, and what the kernel
# makes of it (on Bochs: docs/emulators.md lists where a 286 differs).
program: attack
timeout: 60
---
rx286, test build
attack: cli
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0043:{attacks.cli}
attack: sti
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0043:{attacks.sti}
attack: in
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0043:{attacks.in}
attack: out
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0043:{attacks.out}
attack: hlt
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0043:{attacks.hlt}
attack: lgdt
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0043:{attacks.lgdt}
attack: lidt
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0043:{attacks.lidt}
